From 83e112af9c2e5e0c0f555af93a8284d6dcaf21b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Barbaros=20G=C3=B6ren?= <20913374+7tg@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] input: every signed-in user's DualSense is an XInput
 controller

prospero-win read one DualSense, the foreground user's, as XInput
controller 0, so a game's local multiplayer (Blur's split screen) never
saw a second player. The title now also opens the pads of the other
signed-in users (sceUserServiceGetLoginUserIdList), up to three, as
controllers 1..3: a user keeps a slot while signed in, one who signs in
during the game is found within two seconds, one who signs out frees it.

- native/pw_pad_ps5: PwPadPlayers, pw_pad_players_scan/_close, and the
  login_users op (optional).
- wine/ps5/pw_wine_sink: four pads and rumbles, pw_wine_set_pad_at,
  pw_wine_pad_at, pw_wine_set_rumble_at, pw_wine_rumble_at; the old
  calls are controller 0's. ntdll.prx exports them.
- wine/patches/0471: xinput reads controllers 0..3 through them.
- wine64: reads the players' pads every frame and passes each one's
  rumble on. Bindings, the pointer and Options+Touchpad stay player 1's.
